    "text": "Let slope of the tangent line to a curve at any point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>. If the curve intersects the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>, for which the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the curve, is :",
